@startuml
title Class Search request sequence\n(<<new>> steps added by SearchResultCounter)

skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam ArrowColor #3D405B
skinparam ParticipantBorderColor #3D405B
skinparam ParticipantBackgroundColor #F7F7F2
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #FFF9C4
skinparam NoteBorderColor #E6CC00

autonumber

actor User
participant "classSearch.jsp\n(WebContent/user)" as JSP
participant "Servlet filters\n(HibSessionFilter\nSpring Security\nPageAccessFilter)" as Filters
participant "ClassSearchAction\n(action.ClassSearchAction)" as Action
participant "SessionContext\n(security.SessionContext)" as Security
participant "ClassSearchAction\n::getClasses()" as Query
database "Hibernate ORM\n+ Relational DB" as DB
participant "WebClassListTableBuilder\n(webutil)" as Builder
participant "CourseMessages\n(localization)" as I18N

' ── Initial page load ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

User -> JSP : GET classSearch.action
JSP -> Filters : HTTP request
Filters -> Security : open Hibernate session,\nauthenticate user
Filters -> Action : dispatch to ClassSearchAction.execute()
Action -> Security : checkPermission(Right.Classes)
Action -> JSP : return "showClassSearch"\n(showTable=false — no results yet)
JSP -> User : render search form

' ── User submits search ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────

User -> JSP : POST classSearch.action\n(doit="Search", subjectAreaIds, courseNbr)
JSP -> Filters : HTTP POST
Filters -> Security : authenticate, open Hibernate session
Filters -> Action : dispatch to ClassSearchAction.execute()\n→ searchClasses() → performAction("searchClasses")

Action -> Security : checkPermission(Right.Classes)

Action -> Query : getClasses(form, classAssignmentProxy)
note right of Query
  Builds Hibernate HQL query:
  SELECT c, co FROM Class_ c, CourseOffering co
  WHERE co.subjectArea.uniqueId IN (...)
  AND co.instructionalOffering = c.schedulingSubpart
       .instrOfferingConfig.instructionalOffering
  Applies instructor / itype / room / time filters.
end note
Query -> DB : execute HQL query
DB --> Query : rows (Class_, CourseOffering) pairs
Query --> Action : TreeSet<Object[]> (sorted by ClassCourseComparator)

Action -> Action : classes = form.getClasses()

note over Action #FFF9C4
  <<new>> SearchResultCounter:
  request.setAttribute("resultCount", classes.size())
  Stores integer count in HTTP request scope
  for downstream JSP consumption.
end note

alt classes is empty
  Action -> JSP : addFieldError("searchResult", errorNoRecords())\nreturn "showClassSearch" (showTable=false)
  JSP -> User : render form + "No records found" error
else classes found
  Action -> JSP : return "showClassSearch" (showTable=true)

  JSP -> JSP : evaluate: showTable==true\n&& #request.resultCount != null

  note over JSP #FFF9C4
    <<new>> SearchResultCounter:
    <s:if test="showTable == true && #request.resultCount != null">
      renders <div>Found N classes</div>
    using CourseMessages.foundClasses() via <loc:message>
  end note

  JSP -> I18N : foundClasses() → "Found {0} classes"
  I18N --> JSP : "Found 42 classes" (parameterized)
  JSP -> User : render count banner "Found 42 classes"

  JSP -> Action : call printTable() via OGNL
  Action -> Builder : htmlTableForClasses(context, classAssignment,\n  examAssignment, form, out, backType, backId)
  Builder -> DB : load room / instructor / assignment data
  DB --> Builder : assignment details
  Builder --> JSP : HTML table rows
  JSP -> User : render full class results table
end

' ── Export paths (count still set) ──────────────────────────────────────────

User -> JSP : POST classSearch.action (doit="Export PDF")
JSP -> Action : performAction("exportPdf")
note right of Action
  getClasses() called again.
  resultCount still set in request scope
  (attribute present but JSP not rendered for export).
end note
Action -> DB : HQL query (same as search)
DB --> Action : classes
Action -> Builder : pdfTableForClasses(...)
Builder --> User : PDF file download

note bottom
  Reverse-engineered from ClassSearchAction.java (execute, performAction, getClasses),
  classSearch.jsp, CourseMessages.java, and WebClassListTableBuilder.java.
  <<new>> annotations mark the two lines and one JSP block added by SearchResultCounter.
end note

@enduml
